+For platform.sftp.upload, WTL-SFTP-1 binds the exact local/remote paths, SHA256 and maximum bytes to the consumed host grant. Platform transfer opens a regular local file without following links, checks identity/length and hashes its actual bytes against that approved digest before remote mutation; it rechecks the source, hashes the remote temporary file and verifies the final named result. These are enforced transfer semantics, not a claim that this future transfer has happened. Match the exact sourceArchiveObservations path/hash/byte identity when supplied. SourceArchiver originally hashes the compressed output and re-reads its frozen copy before publishing that association. Candidate upload separately checks the returned byte/hash/path receipt; the build pipeline independently queries task ownership and remote bytes/hash before executing the archive. An upload is data transfer, not execution of archive hooks; execution needs its own full review and isolation. Do not invent a requirement for an already transferred remote checksum before transfer. Changed sources/targets, missing authority, conflicting observations or unreviewed execution still fail.
